    "created_at": "2016-04-12T18:55:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-12T18:55:48Z",
    "body": "And `<xmp>` isn't pre-like in any significant way.  In particular, it doesn't have the automatic strip-first-character-if-it's-a-newline behavior, and is not styled with `whitespace:pre` by default.\n\nThe only similarity is that, semantically, both are often used to mark up examples.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/209052611/reactions",
